    <h1> Members Area </h1>

<p> Welcome to the Members Area!  
    Here registered users can access extra cyber security knowledge, useful tips, and advanced online safety information.  
    This section is designed to help you stay safer online and improve your understanding of cyber security.</p>

<img src="Images/pngtree-users-icon-design-png-image_1015832.png"width="220" /> 

<h2> Extra Safety Tips </h2>
<p> Staying safe online requires good habits and awareness.  
    Following these simple tips can greatly reduce the risk of cyber attacks and stolen information.</p>

<ol>
    <li> Use a different password for every account </li>
    <li> Enable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) </li>
    <li> Avoid suspicious links, emails, and downloads </li>
    <li> Keep your software and devices updated </li>
</ol>

<h2> Spotting Fake Websites </h2>
<p> Cybercriminals often create fake websites that look real in order to steal passwords and personal information.  
    Always check that websites use "https://" and avoid pages with strange links, spelling mistakes, or suspicious pop-ups.</p>

    <img src="Images/2092745.png" width="250"/>
    

<h3> Learn More </h3>
<p> Cyber security is constantly changing, so continuing to learn is very important.  
Visit <a href="https://www.cybrary.it/" target="_blank"> Cybrary </a> for free cyber security learning resources and beginner-friendly courses.</p>
